  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">

      <p>On September 1, US CENTCOM conducted a series of precision strikes against IRGC naval facilities and missile staging areas along the Iranian coastline (AP/Reuters, Sep 1). Later that day, Iranian President Pezeshkian, speaking at the SCO summit in Astana, issued a conditional offer to re-enter a modified MOU framework — contingent on a 72-hour US strike pause and guarantees on sanctions relief (IRNA, Sep 1). The gap between Pezeshkian's preconditions and the US operational posture became apparent within 24 hours: Iran launched approximately 59 ballistic missiles and drones at US naval assets on September 2, and F2 expired at EOD September 3 without the required public Iranian commitment to mediated negotiations. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span>, <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>IRGC forces launched additional strike waves on September 2–3, targeting commercial vessels near Kuwait and UAE waters (Al Jazeera, Sep 3). IRGC spokesman Zolfaghari held a press conference on September 3 confirming that Iranian forces had redeployed Maham-3 and Maham-7 naval mines along southern Hormuz transit channels — formally voiding the CENTCOM mine-free declaration of August 27–28 (GlobalSecurity.org, Sep 4). AIS trackers recorded 11 transits on September 2, 9 on September 3, and 4 on September 4 (Straits.live). Two commercial tankers sustained mine damage in the Sep 2–3 period; at the current traffic trajectory, the 30-vessel 7-day average threshold is not achievable before October 3. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span></p>

      <p>US Vice President Vance stated on September 4 that there would be "no talks with Tehran until it stops shooting at commercial shipping" — a formalized US-side exclusion of any near-term negotiating session (AP/Reuters, Sep 4). Qatar Prime Minister Al-Thani's visit to Tehran on August 27 and Omani Foreign Minister Badr Al-Busaidi's parallel mission produced no scheduled session date and no mediator readout of progress (Al Jazeera, Aug 27–28). Trump waved off a deal concept on September 2. The Oman back-channel relay remains nominally open; no party has issued a readout of a convened session. → moved <span class="cite">F3</span></p>

      <p>The September 3 Haaretz poll registered Yashar at 22 seats and Likud at 21, with bloc totals tied 53-53 — within the alternating 21–23 range observed throughout July–September; no fresh September 4–5 polling data was available at time of writing (Haaretz, Sep 3). The F5 indicator "Likud ≥23 seats" reverted from PARTIAL to NOT_OBSERVED following the sub-threshold result. No coalition alliance was announced. The 52-day horizon to the October 27 vote is insufficient to rule out further movement in either direction. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span></p>

    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 4. SCENARIO MAP ========== -->
