      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (62%):</strong> Active kinetic exchange, IRGC mine redeployment, and mutual diplomatic shutdown (F3=7%, F4=8%) make sustained military escalation — potentially toward direct strikes on Iranian territory or Iranian strikes on Gulf state infrastructure — the modal outcome over the next 30 days.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (28%):</strong> A drawn-out low-intensity conflict in which both sides exchange strikes without reaching a threshold that triggers a new ceasefire cycle; Hormuz remains partially frozen through October, and the Oct 27 Israeli election (F5=42%) drives political caution that prevents further escalation.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (10%):</strong> Requires the Oman back-channel to produce a convened session (F3=7%) or a bilateral halt observed over 72h+, unlocking shipping recovery (FN1=20%) and a mutual cessation framework (FN2=25%) within the 86-day window.</p>
