        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>

      <p>Iranian state media framing through September 3–4 emphasizes Iranian military "precision" and "proportionality" in the September 2 missile-drone salvo, with IRNA characterizing the strikes as a "calibrated response to ongoing American aggression" — language that does not acknowledge civilian shipping damage. IRIB's primetime coverage on September 3 led with Zolfaghari's mine-redeployment announcement framed as a "maritime security operation" restoring "sovereign transit management" in the Persian Gulf; the IRGC Strait Authority fee structure was described as a "legitimate service charge" rather than an illegal toll. Press TV published an op-ed on September 4 characterizing VP Vance's "no talks" statement as proof that "Washington has no genuine interest in diplomacy," offering Pezeshkian's SCO offer as the standard against which US intransigence is measured. Kayhan's editorial line remained maximalist, praising "historic steadfastness" and dismissing the Qatar and Oman missions as "cover for American pressure." Fars reported IRGC Navy chief Admiral Tangsiri as saying Iran was "fully prepared for any scenario in the Persian Gulf." No state outlet acknowledged civilian mine casualties or the tanker strikes. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

    </div>
  </div>

